@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Scientific Evidence";
    ViewData["PublicPage"] = true;
}

<div class="marketing-page evidence-v2">
    <div class="evidence-v2-topline">
        <a class="marketing-back" asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index">← Back to Welcome</a>
    </div>

    <section class="evidence-v2-intro">
        <div class="marketing-kicker">SCIENCE-BACKED. SIMPLE TO LIVE.</div>
        <h1>Feel Better Now. <span>Protect Your Tomorrows.</span></h1>
        <p>Real science supports simple habits that improve how you look, feel, perform, and age.</p>
        <strong>It’s Easy When You Find What Motivates You!</strong>
    </section>

    <section class="evidence-comparison-shell">
        <button class="evidence-image-button" type="button" data-evidence-enlarge aria-label="Enlarge the earlier versus later comparison">
            <img class="theme-image theme-image-light"
                 src="~/images/recomp/evidence-compare-light.webp"
                 alt="Earlier proactive self-care compared with later reactive medical care" />
            <img class="theme-image theme-image-dark"
                 src="~/images/recomp/evidence-compare-dark.webp"
                 alt="Earlier proactive self-care compared with later reactive medical care" />
        </button>
        <div class="evidence-enlarge-hint">↗ Tap or click to enlarge</div>
        <p>
            Movement, resistance training, nutrition, recovery, and energy balance influence many
            modifiable health factors. Working on them earlier can improve the trajectory—and in many
            cases reduce how much intervention is needed later.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="marketing-section">
        <div class="marketing-section-head compact">
            <div class="marketing-kicker">THE EVIDENCE AT A GLANCE</div>
            <h2>A lot of science. A pretty simple daily practice.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="evidence-card-grid-v2">
            <article class="evidence-mini-card">
                <span>01</span>
                <h3>What the evidence supports</h3>
                <p>Training, nutrition, recovery, fitness, and energy balance can improve body-composition and health markers.</p>
                <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38031812/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Representative review →</a>
            </article>
            <article class="evidence-mini-card">
                <span>02</span>
                <h3>Body recomposition can occur</h3>
                <p>Fat loss and lean-mass gain can happen together under the right training and nutrition conditions.</p>
                <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26817506/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Randomized trial →</a>
            </article>
            <article class="evidence-mini-card">
                <span>03</span>
                <h3>Resistance training & protein matter</h3>
                <p>Lifting supplies the muscle-retention signal; adequate protein supplies the building material.</p>
                <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39191151/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Resistance-training evidence →</a>
            </article>
            <article class="evidence-mini-card">
                <span>04</span>
                <h3>Energy balance & recovery matter</h3>
                <p>Fat loss requires an energy deficit, but recovery and adequate fueling help keep training productive.</p>
                <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33095376/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Energy-availability review →</a>
            </article>
            <article class="evidence-mini-card">
                <span>05</span>
                <h3>Simple habits work</h3>
                <p>The best plan is one you can repeat: move, eat well, fuel the work, recover, and keep going.</p>
                <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37491419/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Exercise health evidence →</a>
            </article>
            <article class="evidence-mini-card">
                <span>06</span>
                <h3>What the program does not promise</h3>
                <p>No program guarantees an outcome. Biology, consistency, medication, health status, and starting point matter.</p>
                <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39331324/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">More evidence →</a>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="evidence-bottom-cta">
        <div>
            <div class="marketing-kicker">BUILT ON EVIDENCE</div>
            <h2>Focused on simple living.</h2>
            <p>Move your body. Eat well. Fuel smart. Recover. Repeat.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="marketing-cta" href="/.auth/login/aad?post_login_redirect_uri=/Home/AfterSignIn">Get Started</a>
    </section>

    <p class="evidence-disclaimer">
        Recomp is educational fitness and nutrition software, not medical diagnosis or treatment.
        Medication or treatment decisions belong with a qualified clinician.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="evidence-modal" data-evidence-modal hidden>
    <button type="button" class="evidence-modal-close" data-evidence-close aria-label="Close enlarged comparison">×</button>
    <img class="theme-image theme-image-light" src="~/images/recomp/evidence-compare-light.webp" alt="Enlarged proactive self-care versus reactive medical care comparison" />
    <img class="theme-image theme-image-dark" src="~/images/recomp/evidence-compare-dark.webp" alt="Enlarged proactive self-care versus reactive medical care comparison" />
</div>

<script>
    (() => {
        const open = document.querySelector('[data-evidence-enlarge]');
        const modal = document.querySelector('[data-evidence-modal]');
        const close = document.querySelector('[data-evidence-close]');
        if (!open || !modal || !close) return;

        const hide = () => { modal.hidden = true; document.body.classList.remove('modal-open'); };
        open.addEventListener('click', () => { modal.hidden = false; document.body.classList.add('modal-open'); });
        close.addEventListener('click', hide);
        modal.addEventListener('click', event => { if (event.target === modal) hide(); });
        document.addEventListener('keydown', event => { if (event.key === 'Escape' && !modal.hidden) hide(); });
    })();
</script>
